abstract: >
  The Cognitive Sovereignty Framework is a six-domain model for examining human
  capability, independent judgment, and authority in AI-mediated environments.
  It connects a five-layer threat taxonomy with Cognitive Threat Severity Scores,
  source-backed research, practical safeguards, and declared assessment lenses.
  Cyber Strategy Institute maintains its assessments and preserves their inputs,
  evidence, uncertainty, and revisions for review and future validation.
